# E02 BDI Architecture with two fires side by side (oracle BDIAdjacent: the first fire starts on cells 3 and 4), in
# legacy mode (D89): the patrol puts out the fire on 4, still sees the one on 3 with an empty plan, and both the C# and
# the port stop for good on reading that plan. Exact trace as BDI.rules; the text of the exception is the runtime's, so
# it is counted, not compared ("out of range" is in both).
cover all
fact order (^Starting|^\t\[[\w-]+ -> [\w-]+\]|^Adopting|^GUI|out of range)
fact start ^Starting (\w+)$
fact message ^\t\[([\w-]+) -> ([\w-]+)\]: (.*)$
fact intention ^Adopting new intention: (.*)$
fact gui ^GUI pos=(\d+) ([.FWw]+)$
fact error out of range
same order seq
same start seq
same message seq
same intention seq
same gui seq
# one exception, then nothing: the patrol and the terrain wait for good
check error count == 1
check message count == 34
